    The rule below is the ground truth for where traffic is actually sent:
    cluster-IP rule (KUBE-SVC-NU3EPORMY7BJPWSM):
      -N KUBE-SVC-NU3EPORMY7BJPWSM
      -A KUBE-SVC-NU3EPORMY7BJPWSM ! -s 10.244.0.0/16 -d 10.96.116.237/32 -p tcp -m comment --comment "imesh-demo/backend:http cluster IP" -m tcp --dport 80 -j KUBE-MARK-MASQ
      -A KUBE-SVC-NU3EPORMY7BJPWSM -m comment --comment "imesh-demo/backend:http -> 10.244.1.2:9090" -m statistic --mode random --probability 0.50000000000 -j KUBE-SEP-W63RYVPXPK4XVHZR
      -A KUBE-SVC-NU3EPORMY7BJPWSM -m comment --comment "imesh-demo/backend:http -> 10.244.1.3:9090" -j KUBE-SEP-N5YRTSCBPFTO5KR7
    
    per-endpoint DNAT rules (these contain the real destination port):
      -N KUBE-SEP-W63RYVPXPK4XVHZR
